{"ts": "2026-08-17T10:10:17Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 152, "kind": "message", "text": "I have what I need \u2014 the project uses plain CSS with an established minimal palette, no component library, and existing patterns to extend (AddTask's form pattern, App.jsx's `run()` error handling, the `.task` row layout). Let me verify contrast for the color I'll reuse before writing the doc.\n\nThe existing error color `#a3271d` on white (`#fff`, the `.task` card background) computes to **7.33:1** \u2014 passes AAA, so I can safely reuse it for a compact inline validation message instead of inventing a new color.\n\nNow writing the design doc.", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "text", "session_id": "8ad64417-0536-4ee5-b4e0-1d1bb9f67e6a"}}
{"ts": "2026-08-17T10:11:09Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 153, "kind": "tool_use", "text": "Write", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "tool_use", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01TDqAAfvYgFD2GFT3eZJXMa", "input": {"file_path": "/home/dev/projects/test-project/docs/design.md", "content": "# Design: Edit a task title\n\nTaiga #2 \u00b7 consumes `docs/spec.md`\n\n## Conventions established (before designing anything)\n\n- No component library, no icon set, no design tokens file \u2014 plain CSS in\n  `frontend/src/App.css`, function components, hooks only.\n- Existing button style is a single neutral style (`button { border, white\n  bg, radius 5px }`) with no primary/secondary visual hierarchy \u2014 Done and\n  Delete look the same. Nothing today distinguishes \"safe\" vs \"destructive\"\n  by color.\n- Existing form pattern is `AddTask.jsx`: a `<form onSubmit>` wrapping an\n  `<input>` + submit `<button>`, client-side `.trim()` check before calling\n  the handler, `aria-label` on the input.\n- Existing per-row actions (`TaskList.jsx`) are plain-text buttons with an\n  `aria-label` that includes the task's title (`` `Complete ${task.title}` ``)\n  for screen-reader disambiguation between rows.\n- Existing error surface is a single global banner in `App.jsx` \u2014\n  `<p className=\"error\" role=\"alert\">` \u2014 fed by `run()`'s catch block.\n- Existing color tokens in use: text `#16191c`, border `#ccd2d6`, error text\n  `#a3271d` on error bg `#fbe9e7`, muted `#6b7780`, card bg `#fff`, page bg\n  `#f6f7f8`.\n\n**Decision: introduce no new component, no new color, no new button style.**\nEverything below extends `TaskList.jsx` and `App.css` in place, per the\nspec's affected areas.\n\n## Interaction model\n\n`TaskList` owns edit state locally (per spec: \"per-task edit-mode state\"):\n\n```js\nconst [editingId, setEditingId] = useState(null)\nconst [draft, setDraft] = useState('')\nconst [validationError, setValidationError] = useState(null)\n```\n\n- **Enter edit mode** \u2014 click a task's `Edit` button \u2192\n  `setEditingId(task.id); setDraft(task.title); setValidationError(null)`.\n  The input autofocuses (`autoFocus` \u2014 safe here since it only fires on a\n  direct user click, not on page load).\n- **Opening edit on a different task** \u2014 clicking `Edit` elsewhere just calls\n  `startEdit` again; `editingId`/`draft` are overwritten, so the previous\n  row's unsaved draft is silently discarded. This *is* the resolution to the\n  spec's open question 2 (only one task edits at a time) \u2014 no confirmation\n  dialog, per the spec's stated default.\n- **Cancel** \u2014 `Cancel` button, or `Escape` in the input \u2192\n  `setEditingId(null); setValidationError(null)`. No request sent. The row\n  re-renders from `tasks` (untouched), so the original title reappears with\n  no extra revert logic needed.\n- **Save, empty/whitespace draft (AC4)** \u2014 submit handler trims the draft\n  first, same as `AddTask.jsx` line 8. If empty, **block before calling\n  `onEdit`**: `setValidationError(\"Title can't be empty.\")`, keep\n  `editingId` set, return. No request is sent, focus stays in the input\n  (it never lost focus), the draft the user typed is preserved so they can\n  fix it in place.\n- **Save, valid draft (AC2)** \u2014 trimmed non-empty value \u2192 close edit mode\n  immediately (`setEditingId(null)`), call `onEdit(task.id, trimmed)`. This\n  is optimistic: the row briefly shows the old title until `App.jsx`'s\n  `run()` \u2192 `refresh()` completes, then shows the new one. No new\n  loading-state UI is introduced for this, matching Complete/Delete, which\n  have the same brief-old-value-until-refresh gap today.\n- **Save, oversized draft (AC5)** \u2014 no client-side length check is added\n  (spec non-goal). An over-200-char draft is *not* caught by the empty\n  check, so it takes the same path as a valid save: edit mode closes\n  optimistically, the request goes out, the backend 422s, and the existing\n  global banner in `App.jsx` shows it \u2014 identical to how `AddTask` handles\n  an oversized create today. This means AC5, unlike AC4, does *not* keep\n  edit mode open on rejection \u2014 that asymmetry is intentional: the spec says\n  AC5 should be rejected \"the same way create rejects it today,\" and create\n  has no such behavior either. If this asymmetry is undesirable, the fix is\n  a client-side length guard, which is explicitly out of scope (non-goal:\n  \"No character counter or other new max-length UI\").\n- **Click elsewhere on the page while editing** \u2014 no effect. Edit mode is\n  not exited by blur/click-outside; only explicit Cancel, Escape, Save, or\n  switching to another row's Edit closes it. (Not specified by the spec;\n  chosen because silent data loss on an accidental click is worse than\n  requiring an explicit action.)\n\n## States (per row)\n\n### Display, open task (unchanged baseline)\n\n```\n\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n\u2502 Buy milk                     [ Done ] [ Edit ] [Delete] \u2502\n\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n```\n\n`Edit` is inserted between `Done` and `Delete` \u2014 a modifying action sits\nnext to the other modifying action, and stays spatially separated from the\ndestructive one on its far side (`destructive-emphasis` guideline: keep\ndestructive actions visually distinguishable/separated; nothing here changes\nDelete's own styling, just its neighbor).\n\n### Display, done task\n\n```\n\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n\u2502 S\u0336u\u0336b\u0336m\u0336i\u0336t\u0336 \u0336r\u0336e\u0336p\u0336o\u0336r\u0336t\u0336  (struck through, 0.55 opacity)   [ Edit ] [Delete] \u2502\n\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n```\n\nPer spec open question 1 (default: yes, done tasks stay editable), `Edit`\nrenders unconditionally \u2014 only `Done` is conditional on `!task.done`\n(existing behavior, unchanged).\n\n### Edit mode, just opened\n\n```\n\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n\u2502 [ Buy milk|                    ]   [ Save ] [Cancel]\u2502\n\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n```\n\nInput replaces the `.task-title` span in place (same flex position,\n`flex: 1`). `Save`/`Cancel` replace `Done`/`Edit`/`Delete` in the same slot \u2014\nonly one action set is ever visible per row, so there's no risk of clicking\na stale Delete mid-edit.\n\n### Edit mode, empty/whitespace submitted (AC4)\n\n```\n\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n\u2502 [                                ]   [ Save ] [Cancel]\u2502\n\u2502 Title can't be empty.                                \u2502\n\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n```\n\n- Input gets a `.invalid` class \u2192 border color becomes `#a3271d` (same red\n  as the existing error token). This is a *reinforcing* signal, not the only\n  one (`color-not-only`): the text message is the primary signal and is what\n  a screen reader announces.\n- Error text: `#a3271d` on the card's white background \u2014 **7.33:1**,\n  computed from the actual token (`R163 G39 B29` \u2192 relative luminance\n  0.0933; `(1.0 + 0.05) / (0.0933 + 0.05) = 7.33`). Passes AAA (\u22657:1), well\n  past the 4.5:1 floor.\n- `<p className=\"task-edit-error\" role=\"alert\" id={`edit-error-${task.id}`}>`\n  \u2014 reuses the exact `role=\"alert\"` pattern already in `App.jsx:46`, so it's\n  announced immediately (`aria-live-errors`), rather than inventing a new\n  live-region convention.\n- Input carries `aria-invalid=\"true\"` and\n  `aria-describedby=\"edit-error-${task.id}\"` while the error is shown\n  (`error-clarity`, `focus-management` adjacent: the field stays focused,\n  nothing moves).\n- Message wording states cause plainly (\"Title can't be empty.\") \u2014 no\n  contrived \"how to fix\" clause needed since the fix is self-evident (type\n  something) and the input is right there, already focused.\n- Layout: the error line uses `flex-basis: 100%; order: 1` inside the same\n  flex row, so it drops below the input/buttons without restructuring the\n  `<li>` into a grid or adding a wrapper element.\n\n### Populated list, mixed states\n\nLong titles: the input is a native single-line text field \u2014 no truncation\nneeded (unlike the read-only span, an editable field scrolls its own\noverflow). No `textarea` \u2014 title is and remains a single-line field per\n`TaskIn`.\n\nOne task / many tasks / all-done / all-open: no new empty-state or\nvirtualization concerns \u2014 this feature touches only the per-row action set,\n`TaskList`'s empty-state branch (`EMPTY_COPY`) is untouched.\n\n### Error from the backend (404 deleted-elsewhere, 422 oversized)\n\nReuses the existing global banner exactly as `AddTask`'s create failures do\ntoday \u2014 no new UI:\n\n```\n\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n\u2502 request failed (404)                            \u2502  \u2190 .error, role=\"alert\"\n\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n  Buy milk                     [ Done ] [ Edit ] [Delete]\n```\n\nRow has already reverted to display mode (optimistic close) showing the\npre-edit title, since `refresh()` re-fetches the unchanged store state.\n\n## Keyboard & accessibility\n\n- **Enter** submits (native form-submit behavior, same as `AddTask` \u2014 no\n  explicit `onKeyDown` needed for this one).\n- **Escape** cancels \u2014 needs an explicit `onKeyDown` on the input, since\n  Escape has no native form behavior:\n  `if (e.key === 'Escape') cancelEdit()`.\n- **Tab order**: Save then Cancel, matching DOM/visual order left-to-right \u2014\n  no `tabIndex` overrides needed.\n- **Focus ring**: rely on the browser default (project sets no `outline:\n  none` anywhere today) \u2014 `focus-states` is satisfied for free.\n- **Touch targets**: Save/Cancel/Edit reuse the existing `button` rule\n  unchanged (`padding: 0.5rem 0.8rem`), same as Done/Delete today. That\n  rule's rendered height is under the 44\u00d744 recommendation project-wide \u2014\n  true for every button in this app already, not something this feature\n  introduces or is scoped to fix (non-goal territory: this cycle extends\n  `.task`, it doesn't redesign the button system). Flagging it here so it's\n  a known, pre-existing characteristic rather than a silent gap.\n- **Row gap**: existing `.task` `gap: 0.5rem` (8px) already satisfies\n  `touch-spacing` between the new buttons \u2014 no change needed.\n- Input `aria-label=\"Task title\"` \u2014 reuses `AddTask.jsx`'s exact label\n  (line 20). Fine to reuse verbatim: only one row is ever in edit mode at a\n  time (assumption 2), so there's never a duplicate-label ambiguity for\n  screen readers at any given moment.\n- `Edit`/`Save`/`Cancel` buttons get `aria-label`s that include the task\n  title, matching the existing `Complete ${task.title}` / `Delete\n  ${task.title}` convention:\n  - `aria-label={`Edit ${task.title}`}`\n  - `aria-label={`Save new title for ${task.title}`}`\n  - `aria-label={`Cancel editing ${task.title}`}`\n\n## Exact code changes\n\n**`frontend/src/api.js`** \u2014 add next to `completeTask`/`deleteTask` (after\nline 21):\n```js\nexport const updateTask = (id, title) =>\n  request(`/api/tasks/${id}`, { method: 'PATCH', body: JSON.stringify({ title }) })\n```\n\n**`frontend/src/App.jsx`** \u2014 add `onEdit` prop to `<TaskList>` (alongside\nlines 54-55), same `run()` wiring as the others:\n```jsx\nonEdit={(id, title) => run(() => api.updateTask(id, title))}\n```\n\n**`frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx`** \u2014 replace the static\n`task-title` span (line 15) and the fixed action-button block (lines 16-23)\nwith a conditional: display mode (current markup, plus the new `Edit`\nbutton) vs. edit mode (form with input + Save/Cancel + optional error line),\nswitched on `task.id === editingId`. State and handlers as described in\n\"Interaction model\" above.\n\n**`frontend/src/App.css`** \u2014 add after the `.task-title` rules (after line\n31):\n```css\n.task-edit-input {\n  flex: 1;\n  min-width: 0;\n  padding: 0.55rem 0.7rem;\n  border: 1px solid #ccd2d6;\n  border-radius: 5px;\n  font: inherit;\n}\n.task-edit-input.invalid { border-color: #a3271d; }\n.task-edit-error {\n  flex-basis: 100%;\n  order: 1;\n  color: #a3271d;\n  font-size: 0.85rem;\n  margin: 0.3rem 0 0;\n}\n```\nNo changes to `button` \u2014 Edit/Save/Cancel inherit the existing global rule\n(lines 16-23) unstyled, same as Done/Delete.\n\n## Traceability\n\n| AC | Design element |\n|----|-----------------|\n| 1. Enter edit mode | `Edit` button \u2192 `startEdit()` \u2192 input replaces span, pre-filled, autofocused |\n| 2. Save valid edit | Save/Enter \u2192 trimmed non-empty \u2192 `onEdit(id, trimmed)` via `run()`, edit mode closes |\n| 3. Cancel discards | Cancel/Escape \u2192 `setEditingId(null)`, no request, row re-renders from untouched `tasks` |\n| 4. Empty rejected, correctable in place | Client-side trim check blocks the request; `.task-edit-error`, `role=\"alert\"`, `aria-invalid`/`aria-describedby`; edit mode stays open, input keeps focus and draft |\n| 5. Oversized rejected | No client length check (non-goal); 422 surfaces via existing global `.error` banner, same path as `AddTask` create failures today |\n| 6-8. Backend behavior | No UI surface beyond the above \u2014 covered by `updateTask()`'s use of the existing `request()` error handling |\n\n## Non-goals honored\n\nNo new component file, no new color, no new button visual style, no\ncharacter counter, no undo/history UI, no multi-row edit UI, no click-\noutside-to-save/cancel behavior invented beyond what's needed for AC3/AC4.\n"}, "session_id": "8ad64417-0536-4ee5-b4e0-1d1bb9f67e6a"}}
